Hydra Engine is derived from Ghidra (https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra), the
software reverse engineering framework developed by the National Security Agency, and is
distributed under the same license, the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Ghidra's own
notice is in NOTICE, and the licenses of the third-party components Ghidra uses are in the
licenses/ and GPL/ directories; all of them apply to Hydra Engine unchanged.

What Hydra Engine adds to Ghidra:
  - the HeadlessSession module (Ghidra/Features/HeadlessSession): a shared headless session
    daemon, its Python launcher and client, and their tests;
  - a headless-only build (gradle/hydra/headless.gradle, the buildHeadless task);
  - the repository's own documentation, assets and CI (README.md, NOTICE-HYDRA,
    CHANGELOG.md and the files in .github/);
  - storage integrity after a process kill during a save, in Ghidra's own source: two changed
    files, Ghidra/Framework/DB/src/main/java/db/buffers/LocalManagedBufferFile.java (the new
    version file's header is written and synced before the file is renamed to its final name)
    and Ghidra/Framework/FileSystem/src/main/java/ghidra/framework/store/db/VersionedDatabase.java
    (the newest version is checked when a database is opened), and one added class,
    Ghidra/Framework/FileSystem/src/main/java/ghidra/framework/store/db/VersionFileCheck.java
    (header validation and the quarantine of an unreadable newest version).
Everything else is Ghidra as published by its authors. Ghidra's original README is
README-GHIDRA.md.

